[]\TU/lmtt/m/n/10 (a) A mapping $f$ is called linear if for all $x, y, k$ it is
 the case that $f(x+y)=f(x)+$ $f(y)$ and $f(k x)=k f(x)$. Now let $f$ and $g$ b
e linear mappings. Then $f(g(x+y))=$ $f(g(x)+g(y))=f(g(x))+f(g(y))$ and $f(g(k 
x))=f(k g(x))=k f(g(x))$. Thus, successive executions of linear mappings are a 
linear mapping.[] 
 []


